      "title": "A websocket consumer that overruns its buffer is told it lagged",
      "kind": "ws",
      "fixture": "events-tuned",
      "note": "The flood publishes on a topic this socket did not subscribe to, so every event it carries is filtered away and the lag notification is the only frame the contract allows next. That is what makes `await_frame` honest here: with the flood on the subscribed topic, the frames before the notification would be a race rather than a contract. The fixture's one-deep buffer is what a `count` this small can overrun.",
      "applies": ["rust-http", "python-http", "ts-client"],
      "inapplicable": {
        "rust-ipc": "IPC delivers events as Tauri events, not as websocket frames."
